245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (TheStudent Admission Enquiry Management System is a low-code application developed on the Zoho Creator )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (platform to simplify the collection and management of student admission enquiries. Colleges that record enquiries in paper registers and spreadsheets find it difficult to maintain records, avoid duplicates, track the progress of each student and perform timely follow-ups. This project replaces those methods with a centralised digital system.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (The application contains three connected forms: Course, Student Enquiry and Follow-Up. An online enquiry form validates the data entered by the applicant, checks for duplicate email addresses and phone numbers, and sends an acknowledgement. Admission staff update the status of each enquiry through the stages New, Contacted, Interested, Applied, Admitted and Rejected, and record every follow-up with its date and outcome. Deluge scripts implement validation, notifications and a daily reminder schedule. Reports include list, Kanban and summary views, and an administrator dashboard displays status-wise and course-wise charts. Role-based access separates the tasks of the applicant, admission staff and administrator.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 163 0 R
/E (The report describes the problem, requirements, design, implementation, testing plan, deployment and security aspects of the system, together with an illustrative case study and the complete Deluge source code. The project demonstrates that a low-code platform can be used to build a practical institutional application quickly, with limited programming, and that it can be extended with SMS notifications, online applications and CRM integration.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
